# CQ3 — What are the ordered steps of the melt-quench protocol, with their
#        ensemble, temperature, duration, and cooling rate?
#
# STATUS: DRAFT (PLAN Step 3; cooling-rate semantics and parameter-row shape
#         corrected 2026-08-27 per the independent post-integration review —
#         WORK_LOG.md Entry 29). Syntax-checked only; NOT an executed validation
#         result. Execution belongs to Steps 7-8 (blocked by D-021).
# SOURCE: PLAN.md §6 CQ3; documented instance path: MODELING.md §5.5 (protocol/
#         step/parameter pattern); fixture source: thesis §2.2.4 (pp. 14-15,
#         Fig. 2.1) - 8 steps, per-step NVT/NPT ensembles, 100 ps segments,
#         melt temperature 3000 K (5000 K if SiO2 > 90 mol%), cooling 5 K/ps.
# PATH:   run --obo:RO_0000059 (concretizes)--> melt-quench protocol INSTANCE
#         (BFO 2020 allows a process to concretize a generically dependent
#         continuant; verified reading of the baseline RO_0000059 declaration);
#         run --obo:BFO_0000051 (has part)--> step processes,
#         ordered pairwise by obo:BFO_0000063 (precedes);
#         step --obo:OBI_0000293--> ONE parameter specification per result row:
#         either a statistical ensemble specification (go:GO_0000320) or a
#         further parameter specification (co:PMD_0000013), each
#         --co:PMD_0000077 (specified by value)--> obo:OBI_0001933 value
#         specification carrying obo:OBI_0002135 (has specified value) /
#         obo:OBI_0001937 (has specified numeric value) and obo:IAO_0000039
#         (has measurement unit label).
# EXPECTED ANSWER COLUMNS:
#         ?protocol ?workflow ?run ?step ?stepLabel ?priorStep
#         ?ensembleValue           - "NVT" | "NPT" (A-Box value, not a T-Box individual)
#         ?paramLabel ?paramNumericValue ?paramUnitLabel
#         Each result row binds AT MOST ONE parameter branch: either
#         ?ensembleValue, or the ?paramLabel/?paramNumericValue/?paramUnitLabel
#         group. The cooling rate is answered by the parameter branch (a
#         co:PMD_0000013 instance labelled as the cooling-rate specification,
#         value 5 K/ps + unit; thesis §2.2.4).
# ROW SHAPE (corrected 2026-08-27): the ensemble block and the parameter block
#         were previously independent sibling OPTIONALs, whose join repeated
#         the ensemble value on every parameter row (a cross product). They are
#         now alternative branches (UNION) inside ONE optional group - one row
#         per parameter specification, no sibling-OPTIONAL multiplication. No
#         new ontology relation is introduced by the restructuring.
# ORDERING: the draft returns pairwise ?priorStep/?step precedes edges; the
#         total order is reconstructed by the consumer (or a later query using
#         transitive closure). Step labels in the fixture number the steps.
# GRAPH ASSUMPTION: expected answers assume the ASSERTED graph only -
#         rdfs:subClassOf* traverses asserted subclass axioms; no OWL reasoning
#         (including owl:equivalentClass-based classification) is assumed or
#         claimed; D-021 is pending, so no reasoning result may be claimed.
# BLOCKED PART (D-017, corrected 2026-08-27): GO_0000047 cooling rate is
#         trapped inside the runaway skos:definition literal of GO_0000018 and
#         is NOT a usable declared class until the D-017 repair is approved and
#         executed. The integrated draft matched the attribute slot UNTYPED
#         (?step co:PMD_0000009 ?coolingRateAttribute), which would return ANY
#         process attribute of a step as if it were the cooling rate. The
#         direct process-attribute route (edge + typing) is therefore removed
#         from the SELECT clause and the executable pattern entirely and stays
#         deferred pending the approved D-017 repair - it is kept below as
#         comments only. The prescribed cooling-rate VALUE (5 K/ps, thesis
#         §2.2.4) remains reachable NOW through the ordinary parameter-
#         specification branch of this query (MODELING.md §5.5 trapped-term
#         rule).
# LANGUAGE HANDLING: every returned rdfs:label is filtered with
#         FILTER(lang(?x) = "" || langMatches(lang(?x), "en")) to prevent
#         duplicate English/German rows from multilingual PMDco labels while
#         still admitting untagged fixture literals (fixture labels are
#         English-tagged per D-006/D-031 house style).
# FIXTURE REQUIREMENTS (Step 7): 8 step individuals as parts of the run,
#         pairwise obo:BFO_0000063 edges, per-step ensemble and parameter
#         specifications with obo:OBI_0001933 value specifications; every unit
#         individual referenced by obo:IAO_0000039 (e.g. the kelvin individual)
#         MUST be typed obo:IAO_0000003 "measurement unit label" - the declared
#         range of the functional baseline property obo:IAO_0000039 (verified
#         in go.ttl; requirement added 2026-08-27, MODELING.md §5.5/§6.1).
# NOTES:  go:GO_0000312 (glass simulation workflow) enters through the OPTIONAL
#         workflow block: the workflow definition has the protocol as part.
#         Class IRIs occur only in rdf:type / rdfs:subClassOf* positions.

PREFIX rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX obo:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/>
PREFIX co:   <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/>
PREFIX go:   <https://w3id.org/pmd/glass-ontology/>

SELECT ?protocol ?workflow ?run ?step ?stepLabel ?priorStep
       ?ensembleValue ?paramLabel ?paramNumericValue ?paramUnitLabel
WHERE {
  ?protocol rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* go:GO_0000311 .       # melt-quench protocol
  ?run      obo:RO_0000059 ?protocol .                      # run concretizes protocol
  ?run      rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* go:GO_0000302 .       # glass melt-quench simulation

  OPTIONAL {                                                # workflow definition context
    ?workflow rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* go:GO_0000312 .     # glass simulation workflow
    ?workflow obo:BFO_0000051 ?protocol .                   # has part (ICE part-hood)
  }

  ?run obo:BFO_0000051 ?step .                              # step executions as parts
  OPTIONAL {
    ?step rdfs:label ?stepLabel .
    FILTER ( lang(?stepLabel) = "" || langMatches(lang(?stepLabel), "en") )
  }

  OPTIONAL {                                                # pairwise ordering
    ?priorStep obo:BFO_0000063 ?step .                      # precedes
    ?run obo:BFO_0000051 ?priorStep .
  }

  OPTIONAL {                                                # per-step parameters: ONE optional
    ?step obo:OBI_0000293 ?paramSpec .                      # group; the two branches below are
    ?paramSpec co:PMD_0000077 ?paramVS .                    # alternatives, so each row carries
    ?paramVS rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* obo:OBI_0001933 .    # exactly one parameter specification
    {                                                       # (a) statistical ensemble
      ?paramSpec rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* go:GO_0000320 .  # statistical ensemble specification
      ?paramVS obo:OBI_0002135 ?ensembleValue .             # has specified value ("NVT"/"NPT")
    }
    UNION
    {                                                       # (b) further parameter specification
      ?paramSpec rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* co:PMD_0000013 . # parameter specification
      FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?paramSpec rdf:type/rdfs:subClassOf* go:GO_0000320 . }
      OPTIONAL {
        ?paramSpec rdfs:label ?paramLabel .
        FILTER ( lang(?paramLabel) = "" || langMatches(lang(?paramLabel), "en") )
      }
      OPTIONAL { ?paramVS obo:OBI_0001937 ?paramNumericValue . }
      OPTIONAL {
        ?paramVS obo:IAO_0000039 ?unitLabelIndividual .     # has measurement unit label
        OPTIONAL {
          ?unitLabelIndividual rdfs:label ?paramUnitLabel .
          FILTER ( lang(?paramUnitLabel) = "" || langMatches(lang(?paramUnitLabel), "en") )
        }
      }
    }
  }

  # DEFERRED (D-017) - direct process-attribute route. NOT part of the
  # executable pattern: an untyped co:PMD_0000009 match would return ANY
  # process attribute of the step, and the typing class go:GO_0000047 is
  # trapped inside the runaway GO_0000018 literal until the approved repair.
  # Activate BOTH lines together only after the approved D-017 repair:
  # OPTIONAL {
  #   ?step co:PMD_0000009 ?coolingRateAttribute .          # has process attribute
  #   ?coolingRateAttribute rdf:type go:GO_0000047 .        # cooling rate (trapped; D-017)
  # }
}
ORDER BY ?run ?step
